      },
      "message": "fix(ui): the vise dialog says a setup needs its stock before a fit, and where the vise will land\n\nThe vise grips the stock, not the imported model. With no stock body the\ndialog says so before Place, greys Fit with its reason, offers the Stock\npage and shows the position rows; with a stock it says where the vise\nlands and how far the jaws open (one app derivation, vise_fit, shared\nwith InsertVise). The three no-stock refusals lose the 'invalid\nparameters:' prefix and say what to do. The browser's Stock row reads\n'not set' while the stock has no body.\n\nFixes #1105\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
